/* The tutor courses (course.html): a whole course, session by session, for a tutor (or a parent) taking
   one pupil to an exam. The first is GCSE maths, grade 1 to grade 3 on the Foundation tier: 60 one-hour
   sessions, two a week for 30 weeks, from a baseline check to two full sets of mock papers.

   This file is the plan and the tutor's notes, written by hand. The questions are not here: course.js
   draws them from the GCSE climb's question bank (PopActivities.examBank in activities.js) when the
   course is made, so every print has new numbers and its own mark schemes.

   A session:
     t       title
     kind    teach (the default), start, check, mock, review, skills
     from    [[topic id, [skills from that topic]], ...]: what the session teaches (teach sessions)
     aim     "We are learning to ..."
     keys    what to teach: the points to make and the method to model
     slips   the mistakes to look out for
     ask     a question to ask, and what a good answer says
     help    if they're stuck; push: if they're flying
     home    homework, after the online practice
     merge   true when the session can share a longer session with the one before (fewer weeks)
   Other kinds name what they use: check and review sessions list topics, mock sessions their set and
   paper, and start and skills sessions the climb's existing sheets (paper-gx-...). */
